IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vet-training`

-- Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask about apprenticeships,
-- traineeships and VET courses, with the seat and the situation as parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. Part 7 is written mostly to the employer and the registered training provider; the baseline (vet-training.l4)
-- turned it into the apprentice's questions. Here three people ask:
--   - the apprentice or trainee, or the person about to become one, such as a school leaver going to TAFE: the
--     baseline's seat (all 30 of its questions);
--   - the employer of an apprentice or trainee, or a person about to take one on: the duties of ss 60D(2), (3), 60F(2)
--     and 60G(2), the changes of s 60E(4) and s 60F(4), the chief executive's approval under s 60G(3), the end of the
--     employment (s 60H) and the appeals (ss 60F(8), 60G(4)), all from the baseline's rules;
--   - a training provider: the duties of s 58A(1)-(3) and s 60D(1), with s 60I, from the baseline's rules.
-- The chief executive, the Minister, the Training Accreditation Council and the Industrial Relations Commission are never
-- seats: what they may or must do appears as what it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when the
-- situation does not hold, without reading anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, with the
-- same name, type and @desc, so the form asks it once. There is one, for the apprentice and the employer:
--   - `where the training contract stands` (`Where the training contract stands`): no training contract and none
--     proposed; one proposed or signed but not registered yet; one registered. The Act ties Part 7 Divisions 2 and 3 to
--     the training contract, and s 60F(1) ties its commencement to registration ("does not commence until it is
--     registered"). So the questions about what the contract is, who signs and lodges it, and its registration do not
--     arise with no contract; the questions of a contract that has commenced -- changing it (s 60E(4), s 60F(4)),
--     ending it (s 60G), cancelling its registration (s 60F(5)), disputes under it (s 60(f)) and what follows its end
--     (s 60H(2)) -- arise only once it is registered; the employer's duty to lodge (s 60F(2)) and the chief executive's
--     power to refuse registration (s 60F(3)) arise only before.
-- The questions about a course, a qualification and its class, and the appeals and fines, arise in every situation of
-- their role and take no situation input. The provider has no situation input.
--
-- The rules are in vet-training.l4. This module calls them and restates none; for the apprentice each answer is the
-- baseline export's own answer, wrapped. For the employer and the provider, inputs about the apprentice are put in the
-- third person and mapped value for value onto the baseline's first-person types; every map lists every value with no
-- OTHERWISE. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one`
    `I employ an apprentice or trainee, or am about to take one on`
    `I run a training provider`

DECLARE `Where the training contract stands` IS ONE OF
    `there is no training contract, and none is proposed`
    `a training contract is proposed or signed, but not registered yet`
    `the training contract has been registered`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

-- The apprentice's answers: the baseline's own answer types, with `does not arise for you`.
DECLARE `Who must lodge, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `who must lodge` IS A Party

DECLARE `Which prevails, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `which prevails` IS A `Which prevails`

DECLARE `Who may make it, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `who may make it` IS A `Who may make it`

DECLARE `What the chief executive must do, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `what the chief executive must do` IS A `What the chief executive must do`

DECLARE `Where my dispute goes, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `where it goes` IS A `Where my dispute goes`

-- The employer's answer and inputs, in the employer's voice, mapped value for value onto the baseline's.
DECLARE `Who may make the change, for the employer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the apprentice and I together`
    `either the apprentice or I, alone`
    `I alone, to another person who employs the apprentice`

DECLARE `The reason I give` IS ONE OF
    `I have ceased or am about to cease business`
    `a substantial change of circumstances since signing means I cannot fulfil the contract`
    `the apprentice has engaged in serious misconduct`
    `a matter prescribed by the regulations`
    `some other reason`

DECLARE `The decision I am dissatisfied with` IS ONE OF
    `the chief executive refusing to register the training contract`
    `the chief executive refusing to register a variation`
    `the chief executive cancelling the contract's registration`
    `the chief executive approving my termination of the contract`
    `the chief executive refusing to approve my termination of the contract`

DECLARE `The employer's offence` IS ONE OF
    `training an employee for a class A or B qualification outside a training contract (s 60D(3))`
    `putting an employee on a training contract for a class C qualification (s 60D(2))`
    `failing to lodge a training contract (s 60F(2))`
    `ending a training contract after probation without consent or approval (s 60G(2))`

-- The provider's facts about the person it would confer a qualification on (s 60D(1), s 60I), in the third person.
DECLARE `The person's completion` HAS
    `they fulfilled their obligations under a registered training contract` IS A BOOLEAN           -- s 60D(1)(a)
    `they completed an approved VET course for it` IS A BOOLEAN                                    -- s 5(1)
    `I assessed them and am satisfied they have the skills and competency` IS A BOOLEAN             -- s 60I
    `their skills come from training with an employer and other learning` IS A BOOLEAN             -- s 60I(1), class A only

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The situation helpers and the maps list every value and have no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31: a CONSIDER with
-- OTHERWISE takes the OTHERWISE branch for an ASSUMEd value instead of failing, so a case could not show the value was not
-- read).
GIVEN `the contract` IS A `Where the training contract stands`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is no training contract` IF
    CONSIDER `the contract`
    WHEN `there is no training contract, and none is proposed` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a training contract is proposed or signed, but not registered yet` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the training contract has been registered` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the contract` IS A `Where the training contract stands`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the training contract is not registered` IF
    CONSIDER `the contract`
    WHEN `there is no training contract, and none is proposed` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a training contract is proposed or signed, but not registered yet` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the training contract has been registered` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the contract` IS A `Where the training contract stands`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the training contract is not proposed and unregistered` IF
    CONSIDER `the contract`
    WHEN `there is no training contract, and none is proposed` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a training contract is proposed or signed, but not registered yet` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the training contract has been registered` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `who` IS A `Who may make it`
GIVETH A `Who may make the change, for the employer`
`for the employer, who may make it` `who` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `my employer and I together` THEN `the apprentice and I together`
    WHEN `either my employer or I, alone` THEN `either the apprentice or I, alone`
    WHEN `my employer alone, to another person who employs me` THEN `I alone, to another person who employs the apprentice`

GIVEN `the reason` IS A `The reason I give`
GIVETH A `My employer's reason`
`the baseline's reason for` `the reason` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `I have ceased or am about to cease business` THEN `my employer has ceased or is about to cease business`
    WHEN `a substantial change of circumstances since signing means I cannot fulfil the contract` THEN `a substantial change of circumstances since signing means my employer cannot fulfil the contract`
    WHEN `the apprentice has engaged in serious misconduct` THEN `I have engaged in serious misconduct`
    WHEN `a matter prescribed by the regulations` THEN `a matter prescribed by the regulations`
    WHEN `some other reason` THEN `some other reason`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision I am dissatisfied with`
GIVETH A Decision
`the baseline's decision for` `the decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `the chief executive refusing to register the training contract` THEN `the chief executive refusing to register my contract`
    WHEN `the chief executive refusing to register a variation` THEN `the chief executive refusing to register a variation`
    WHEN `the chief executive cancelling the contract's registration` THEN `the chief executive cancelling my contract's registration`
    WHEN `the chief executive approving my termination of the contract` THEN `the chief executive approving my employer's termination`
    WHEN `the chief executive refusing to approve my termination of the contract` THEN `the chief executive refusing to approve a termination`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `The employer's offence`
GIVETH AN Offence
`the baseline's offence for` `the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `training an employee for a class A or B qualification outside a training contract (s 60D(3))` THEN `training me for a class A or B qualification outside a training contract (s 60D(3))`
    WHEN `putting an employee on a training contract for a class C qualification (s 60D(2))` THEN `putting me on a training contract for a class C qualification (s 60D(2))`
    WHEN `failing to lodge a training contract (s 60F(2))` THEN `failing to lodge my training contract (s 60F(2))`
    WHEN `ending a training contract after probation without consent or approval (s 60G(2))` THEN `ending my training contract after probation without consent or approval (s 60G(2))`

GIVEN `done` IS A `The person's completion`
GIVETH A `My completion`
`the baseline's completion for` `done` MEANS
    `My completion` WITH
        `I fulfilled my obligations under a registered training contract`          IS `done`'s `they fulfilled their obligations under a registered training contract`
        `I completed an approved VET course for it`                                IS `done`'s `they completed an approved VET course for it`
        `my provider assessed me and is satisfied I have the skills and competency` IS `done`'s `I assessed them and am satisfied they have the skills and competency`
        `my skills come from training with an employer and other learning`         IS `done`'s `their skills come from training with an employer and other learning`

-- The employer's facts about a termination, put into the baseline's record.
GIVEN `permitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `probation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My termination`
`the baseline's termination for` `permitted` `probation` `expired` `consented` `approved` MEANS
    `My termination` WITH
        `the regulations permit it`           IS `permitted`
        `my contract has a probation period`  IS `probation`
        `the probation period has expired`    IS `expired`
        `I consented`                         IS `consented`
        `the chief executive approved it`     IS `approved`

§§ `For the apprentice or trainee, or the person about to become one`

§§§ `ss 5, 58A -- my course and my provider`

@export Is my course an approved VET course (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 5(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `accredited by the Training Accreditation Council` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Training Accreditation Council has accredited the course under Part 7A
      `accredited under a corresponding law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the course is accredited under another State's or Territory's corresponding law
      `prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations prescribe the course
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my course an approved VET course, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN `yes if` (`Is my course an approved VET course` `accredited by the Training Accreditation Council` `accredited under a corresponding law` `prescribed by the regulations`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my provider offer me this approved VET course (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 58A(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my provider` IS A `My provider` @desc Who is providing the course, and on what registration
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my provider offer me this course, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN `yes if` (`May my provider offer me this course` `my provider`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 60C, 60D, 60I -- which qualifications go through a training contract`

@export May my employer put me on a training contract for this qualification (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60D(2), 60E(1), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the class` IS A `Qualification class` @desc How the Minister has classified the qualification
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my employer put me on a training contract for this qualification` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN `yes if` (`May my employer put me on a training contract for it` `the class`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my employer train me for this qualification without a training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60D(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the class` IS A `Qualification class` @desc How the Minister has classified the qualification
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my employer train me for this qualification without a training contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN `yes if` (`May my employer train me for it without a training contract` `the class`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I get this qualification this way (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60C(3), (4), 60D(1), 60I)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the class` IS A `Qualification class` @desc How the Minister has classified the qualification
      `the route` IS A Route @desc The way you would get the qualification
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I get this qualification this way, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN `yes if` (`Can I get this qualification this way` `the class` `the route`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 60, 60A, 60B, 60E -- what my training contract is, and who signs it`

@export Is my contract a training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60A, 60E(1)-(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `my contract` IS A `My contract` @desc What your contract says and who has signed it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my contract a training contract, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `there is no training contract` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is my contract a training contract` `my contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I an apprentice under Part 7 (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `my contract` IS A `My contract` @desc What your contract says and who has signed it
      `I am named in it as the person to be trained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract names you as the person who will be trained under it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I an apprentice under Part 7, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `there is no training contract` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I an apprentice under Part 7` `my contract` `I am named in it as the person to be trained`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my training time count as working time, including for pay (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60E(1)(a)(iv))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `my contract` IS A `My contract` @desc What your contract says and who has signed it
      `where` IS A `Where I am training` @desc Where you are being trained or assessed
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my training time count as working time, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `there is no training contract` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does my training time count as working time` `my contract` `where`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I sign my training contract on my own (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60(b), (c), 60E(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years when you sign
      `the regulations give a person my age capacity to sign` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations under s 60(c) give a person under 18 of your age capacity to enter into a training contract
      `the regulations require a parent or guardian to sign too` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations on the form of the contract require a parent or guardian of a person your age to sign as well
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I sign my training contract on my own, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `there is no training contract` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can I sign my training contract on my own` `my age` `the regulations give a person my age capacity to sign` `the regulations require a parent or guardian to sign too`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Which prevails, Part 7 or my award (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `they are inconsistent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a provision of Part 7 or its regulations is inconsistent with your award, industrial agreement or the Industrial Relations Act 1979
GIVETH A `Which prevails, if it arises`
`Which prevails, Part 7 or my award, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `there is no training contract` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` (`Which prevails, Part 7 or my award` `they are inconsistent`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 60F -- registration: when my contract starts`

@export Has my training contract started (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60F(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `the chief executive has registered it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the chief executive has registered your training contract
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Has my training contract started, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `there is no training contract` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Has my training contract started` `the chief executive has registered it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the chief executive refuse to register my training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60F(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `my lodgement` IS A `My lodgement` @desc How your contract was lodged and what the chief executive has found
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my contract be refused registration, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not proposed and unregistered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my contract be refused registration` `my lodgement`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Who must lodge my training contract for registration (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60F(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
GIVETH A `Who must lodge, if it arises`
`Who must lodge my training contract, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not proposed and unregistered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` `Who must lodge my training contract`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 60E(4), 60F(4) -- suspending, varying and transferring my contract`

@export Who may make this change to my training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60E(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `the change` IS A Change @desc The change to your training contract
GIVETH A `Who may make it, if it arises`
`Who may make this change, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not registered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` (`Who may make this change` `the change`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my training contract be transferred to this new employer (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60E(4)(c))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `my current employer assigns it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is your current employer who assigns the contract
      `the new employer employs me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person it is assigned to employs you
      `the regulations permit the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations allow this assignment
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my contract be transferred to this employer, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not registered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my contract be transferred to this employer` `my current employer assigns it` `the new employer employs me` `the regulations permit the transfer`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I suspend my training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60E(4)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `the regulations permit the suspension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations allow the suspension
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I suspend my training contract, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not registered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I suspend my training contract` `the regulations permit the suspension`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must this change to my training contract be lodged with the chief executive for registration (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60F(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `the change` IS A Change @desc The change to your training contract
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must this change to my contract be lodged, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not registered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must this change be lodged for registration` `the change`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 60G -- probation and termination`

@export Am I protected from my employer ending my contract without my consent (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60G(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `my contract has a probation period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract has a probation period
      `the probation period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that probation period has ended
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I protected from termination without my consent, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not registered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I protected from termination without my consent` `my contract has a probation period` `the probation period has expired`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my training contract be terminated by this party (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60G(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `who` IS A Party @desc Who is ending the contract
      `the termination` IS A `My termination` @desc The facts about the termination
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my contract be terminated, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not registered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my contract be terminated` `who` `the termination`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Has my employer committed an offence by ending my contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60G(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `the termination` IS A `My termination` @desc The facts about the termination
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Has my employer committed an offence by ending my contract, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not registered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Has my employer committed an offence by ending my contract` `the termination`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What must the chief executive do when my employer asks to end my contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60G(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `the reason` IS A `My employer's reason` @desc The reason your employer gives for ending the contract
GIVETH A `What the chief executive must do, if it arises`
`What must the chief executive do, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not registered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` (`What must the chief executive do` `the reason`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 60F(5)-(6), 60H -- when my contract ends`

@export Is my training contract in effect (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60F(1), (6), 60H(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `the status` IS A `My contract's status` @desc What has happened to your contract
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my training contract in effect, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `there is no training contract` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is my training contract in effect` `the status`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I still employed under my training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60H)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `the status` IS A `My contract's status` @desc What has happened to your contract
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I still employed under my training contract, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `there is no training contract` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I still employed under my training contract` `the status`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my employer and I agree a new employment arrangement after my training contract ends (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60H(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May we agree a new arrangement after it ends, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not registered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` `May we agree a new arrangement after it ends`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the chief executive cancel my contract's registration (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60F(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `a prescribed reason applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reason prescribed in the regulations for cancelling registration applies
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my contract's registration be cancelled, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not registered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my contract's registration be cancelled` `a prescribed reason applies`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 58A(3), 60D(1), 60I -- finishing: getting my qualification`

@export May my training provider confer this qualification on me (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 58A(3), 60D(1), 60I)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the class` IS A `Qualification class` @desc How the Minister has classified the qualification
      `my provider` IS A `My provider` @desc Who is providing the course, and on what registration
      `my completion` IS A `My completion` @desc What you have done towards the qualification
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my provider confer this qualification, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN `yes if` (`May my provider confer this qualification` `the class` `my provider` `my completion`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 60, 60F(8)-(9), 60G(4)-(5) -- appeals and disputes`

@export May I appeal this decision to the Western Australian Industrial Relations Commission (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60(i), 60F(8), 60G(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the decision` IS A Decision @desc The decision you are dissatisfied with
      `the regulations give an appeal against refusing a qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations under s 60(i) give a right of appeal against refusing a qualification
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I appeal to the Commission, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN `yes if` (`May I appeal to the Commission` `the decision` `the regulations give an appeal against refusing a qualification`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the Commission do this on my appeal (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60F(9), 60G(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the outcome` IS AN `Appeal outcome` @desc What you want the Commission to do
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Commission do this on my appeal, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN `yes if` (`May the Commission do this on my appeal` `the outcome`)
    WHEN `I employ an apprentice or trainee, or am about to take one on` THEN `yes if` (`May the Commission do this on my appeal` `the outcome`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Where can I take a dispute with my employer under my training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60(f))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `the regulations provide for resolution by the chief executive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations provide for the chief executive (or an appointee) to resolve disputes under training contracts
      `the regulations give an appeal to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations give a party aggrieved by that decision an appeal to the Industrial Relations Commission
GIVETH A `Where my dispute goes, if it arises`
`Where can I take my dispute, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not registered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` (`Where can I take my dispute` `the regulations provide for resolution by the chief executive` `the regulations give an appeal to the Commission`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 58A, 60D, 60F(2), 60G(2) -- penalties`

@export What is the most the offender can be fined, in dollars (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 58A, 60D, 60F(2), 60G(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the offence` IS AN Offence @desc The offence
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most the offender can be fined, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one` THEN amount (`What is the most the offender can be fined` `the offence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the employer of an apprentice or trainee, or a person about to take one on`

§§§ `s 60D(2), (3) -- which qualifications go through a training contract`

@export May I put my employee on a training contract for this qualification (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60D(2), 60E(1), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the class` IS A `Qualification class` @desc How the Minister has classified the qualification
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I put my employee on a training contract for this qualification` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ an apprentice or trainee, or am about to take one on` THEN `yes if` (`May my employer put me on a training contract for it` `the class`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I train my employee for this qualification without a training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60D(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the class` IS A `Qualification class` @desc How the Minister has classified the qualification
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I train my employee for this qualification without a training contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ an apprentice or trainee, or am about to take one on` THEN `yes if` (`May my employer train me for it without a training contract` `the class`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 60A, 60E, 60F -- the contract, and lodging it`

@export Is our contract a training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60A, 60E(1)-(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `the contract` IS A `My contract` @desc What the contract says and who has signed it (the record's "I" is the apprentice or trainee)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is our contract a training contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ an apprentice or trainee, or am about to take one on` THEN
        IF `there is no training contract` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is my contract a training contract` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I lodge the training contract with the chief executive for registration, on pain of a fine (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60F(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I lodge the training contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ an apprentice or trainee, or am about to take one on` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not proposed and unregistered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`is my employer` `Who must lodge my training contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the chief executive refuse to register the training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60F(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `the lodgement` IS A `My lodgement` @desc How the contract was lodged and what the chief executive has found (the record's "my employer" is you, "I" the apprentice)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the training contract be refused registration` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ an apprentice or trainee, or am about to take one on` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not proposed and unregistered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my contract be refused registration` `the lodgement`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 60E(4), 60F(4) -- changing the contract`

@export Who may make this change to the training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60E(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `the change` IS A Change @desc The change to your training contract
GIVETH A `Who may make the change, for the employer`
`Who may make this change to the training contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ an apprentice or trainee, or am about to take one on` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not registered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `for the employer, who may make it` (`Who may make this change` `the change`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I transfer the training contract to another person who employs the apprentice (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60E(4)(c))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `the new employer employs the apprentice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you would assign the contract to employs the apprentice or trainee
      `the regulations permit the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations allow this assignment
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I transfer the training contract to another employer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ an apprentice or trainee, or am about to take one on` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not registered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my contract be transferred to this employer` TRUE `the new employer employs the apprentice` `the regulations permit the transfer`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must this change to the training contract be lodged with the chief executive for registration (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60F(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `the change` IS A Change @desc The change to your training contract
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must this change to the training contract be lodged` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ an apprentice or trainee, or am about to take one on` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not registered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must this change be lodged for registration` `the change`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 60G -- ending the contract`

@export May I end the training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60G(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `the regulations permit the termination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations allow the training contract to be ended
      `the contract has a probation period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the training contract has a probation period
      `the probation period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that probation period has ended
      `the apprentice consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the apprentice or trainee has consented to the termination
      `the chief executive approved the termination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the chief executive has approved the termination
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I end the training contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ an apprentice or trainee, or am about to take one on` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not registered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my contract be terminated` `my employer` (`the baseline's termination for` `the regulations permit the termination` `the contract has a probation period` `the probation period has expired` `the apprentice consented` `the chief executive approved the termination`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Would I commit an offence by ending the training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60G(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `the contract has a probation period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the training contract has a probation period
      `the probation period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that probation period has ended
      `the apprentice consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the apprentice or trainee has consented to the termination
      `the chief executive approved the termination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the chief executive has approved the termination
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Would I commit an offence by ending the training contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ an apprentice or trainee, or am about to take one on` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not registered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Has my employer committed an offence by ending my contract` (`the baseline's termination for` TRUE `the contract has a probation period` `the probation period has expired` `the apprentice consented` `the chief executive approved the termination`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the chief executive approve my ending the training contract for this reason (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60G(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `my reason` IS A `The reason I give` @desc The reason you give for ending the training contract
GIVETH A `What the chief executive must do, if it arises`
`What must the chief executive do with my request to end the contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ an apprentice or trainee, or am about to take one on` THEN
        IF `the training contract is not registered` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` (`What must the chief executive do` (`the baseline's reason for` `my reason`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 60F(6), 60H -- when the contract ends`

@export Does the apprentice's employment under the training contract continue (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60F(6), 60H(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the training contract stands` IS A `Where the training contract stands` @desc Whether there is a training contract between the apprentice or trainee and the employer, and whether the chief executive has registered it
      `the status` IS A `My contract's status` @desc What has happened to your contract
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the apprentice's employment under the contract continue` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ an apprentice or trainee, or am about to take one on` THEN
        IF `there is no training contract` `where the training contract stands`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I still employed under my training contract` `the status`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 60F(8)-(9), 60G(4)-(5) -- appeals`

@export May I appeal this decision of the chief executive to the Western Australian Industrial Relations Commission (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60F(8), 60G(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the decision I am dissatisfied with` IS A `The decision I am dissatisfied with` @desc The decision of the chief executive you are dissatisfied with
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I as employer appeal to the Commission` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ an apprentice or trainee, or am about to take one on` THEN `yes if` (`May I appeal to the Commission` (`the baseline's decision for` `the decision I am dissatisfied with`) FALSE)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 60D, 60F(2), 60G(2) -- penalties`

@export What is the most I can be fined for this offence, in dollars (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60D, 60F(2), 60G(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer's offence` IS A `The employer's offence` @desc The offence
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined as employer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ an apprentice or trainee, or am about to take one on` THEN amount (`What is the most the offender can be fined` (`the baseline's offence for` `the employer's offence`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

